cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "How far is the ETH refutation from practice? Break-even sizes of the Appendix D route"
abstract: >-
  Break-even sizes of the tensor-contraction route in Appendix D of OpenAI's preprint
  "The Exponential Time Hypothesis is False" against the best known algorithms, with the
  frozen cost model, the referee, the loop's code and the ledger that produced them. On 3-CNF
  formulas in which every variable occurs at most three times, the route beats the best
  counting bound known for that class, 2^(n/3), only from about 10^158 variables, and brute
  force from about 10^28. The thresholds are feasible values of a frozen cost model, not
  proved minima.
